{"gene":"PTPN11","uniprot":"Q06124","proteinName":"tyrosine-protein phosphatase non-receptor type 11 isoform 1","function":"Acts downstream of various receptor and cytoplasmic protein tyrosine kinases to participate in the signal transduction from the cell surface to the nucleus. Positively regulates MAPK signal transduction pathway. Dephosphorylates GAB1, ARHGAP35 and EGFR. Dephosphorylates ROCK2 at 'Tyr-722' resulting in stimulation of its RhoA binding activity. Dephosphorylates CDC73. Dephosphorylates SOX9 on tyrosine residues, leading to inactivate SOX9 and promote ossification. Dephosphorylates tyrosine-phosphorylated NEDD9/CAS-L. Acts as an effector of PDCD1-mediated inhibition of T-cell response: recruited by phosphorylated PDCD1, mediating dephosphorylation of key T-cell receptor (TCR) proximal signaling molecules, leading to TCR signaling inhibition","pathwayComment":null,"pathways":[{"id":"R-HSA-1280218","name":"Adaptive Immune System","evidence":"TAS","depth":2,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-422475","name":"Axon guidance","evidence":"TAS","depth":3,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-202733","name":"Cell surface interactions at the vascular wall","evidence":"TAS","depth":2,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-9927353","name":"Co-inhibition by BTLA","evidence":"TAS","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-389513","name":"Co-inhibition by CTLA4","evidence":"TAS","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-389948","name":"Co-inhibition by PD-1","evidence":"TAS","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-2219530","name":"Constitutive Signaling by Aberrant PI3K in Cancer","evidence":"TAS","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-1280215","name":"Cytokine Signaling in Immune system","evidence":"IEA","depth":2,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-5663202","name":"Diseases of signal transduction by growth factor receptors and second messengers","evidence":"TAS","depth":2,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-186763","name":"Downstream signal transduction","evidence":"TAS","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-9607240","name":"FLT3 Signa